            <section class="info-section" id="what">
                <h2>1. What Willow is</h2>
                <p>Willow Banking Corp. is a fictional company and this site is a software demonstration. It is not a bank, broker-dealer, investment adviser, lender, money transmitter or crypto-asset service provider, and it does not offer any real financial product.</p>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="simulated">
                <h2>2. Simulated money and activity</h2>
                <p>Balances, deposits, withdrawals, payments, transfers, cards, currency conversions, invoices, loans and investment trades are database records only. Nothing is sent to a bank, card network, exchange or blockchain, and simulated balances can never be withdrawn as real money.</p>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="information">
                <h2>3. Market data and estimates</h2>
                <p>Market prices are delayed third-party data provided for illustration and may be incomplete, late or unavailable. Exchange rates, loan figures and portfolio projections are indicative estimates. None of it is investment, tax, legal or lending advice, and none of it is an offer.</p>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="use">
                <h2>4. Using the demo</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Use fictional personal details and a password you don’t use anywhere else.</li>
                    <li>Don’t enter real card numbers, identity documents or bank details.</li>
                    <li>Don’t try to break, overload or gain access to other people’s profiles.</li>
                    <li>Keep your sign-in and recovery codes to yourself; you are responsible for activity on your demo profile.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="availability">
                <h2>5. Availability and changes</h2>
                <p>The demo may change, reset or go offline at any time, and stored data may be lost. Administrators of an instance may suspend or close profiles that misuse it.</p>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="warranty">
                <h2>6. No warranty</h2>
                <p>The software is provided as is, without warranties of any kind. Because no real money or services are involved, no compensation, deposit protection or investor protection scheme applies.</p>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="questions">
